ually  sometimes what depression looks like in  teenagers  if a parent is worried they should  absolutely consult with their physician  or a mental health professional  to check things out lisa how do you deal  with the  with with the sort of the constantly  changing landscape we're looking at  right now i mean  a lot of kids were told they'd be going  back into the class then all of a sudden  the school changed its mind  it's shifting all the time it we're all  dealing with it but i think  that's really kids are used to routine  they're usually trying we try to give  them a routine they need routines yeah  you know i think it's pretty good to  think two weeks out you know what is  this week looking to look like maybe  what is next week going to look like and  even within those  short time frames to create routines  that in the day-to-day there can be some  predictability  even if there can't be predictability  over a broader scope  and one of the things i love about kids  and teenagers is they are flexible  they're actually more flexible than  grown-ups  so if the grown-ups can have some  confidence that kids will figure this  out and be able to adapt as this  continues to change on this  on all of us i think kids will figure it  out and we can count on them for that  all right lisa i think you're leaving  everyone feeling a lot calmer this year  we appreciate that  much the job to help people feel good  that's what psychologists are supposed  to do  well mission accomplishments bravo

